234	     * the national digits grouped in threes, e.g. {@code "+61412345678"} becomes
235	     * {@code "+61 412 345 678"}. The country code is a single {@code '1'} for NANP ({@code +1}) numbers
236	     * and two digits otherwise (covering the {@code +61} numbers the app stores). Returns the value
237	     * unchanged when it is absent or not a well-formed E.164 number, leaving raw {@code telephone}
238	     * untouched.
